WEBVTT

00:03.840 --> 00:04.810
It's fine...

00:04.810 --> 00:08.240
It'll all work out if I persevere.

01:31.150 --> 01:35.280
Midarezaki Kyouka, age 20. All of a sudden I have to fight against the evil that tries to take over the world.

01:35.280 --> 01:36.650
Everyone, let's go!

01:36.650 --> 01:38.200
We'll serve for the Earth's future, meow!

01:58.590 --> 01:59.800
Question one.

01:59.800 --> 02:02.050
Why are we under attack?

02:02.050 --> 02:04.060
I don't know. I cannot come up with
an answer with the given information.

02:04.060 --> 02:05.310
Then question two.

02:05.310 --> 02:07.140
What are they?

02:07.140 --> 02:08.980
Probably mass produced biological weapons.

02:08.980 --> 02:12.310
From the ones I know, they could be the Green Twenty-seven.

02:12.310 --> 02:13.900
*clap clap clap*

02:13.900 --> 02:15.400
As expected of you, Thirteen.

02:15.880 --> 02:18.740
Ciao, Thirteen. It's your daddy.

02:17.670 --> 02:18.740
Dr. Gebok.

02:18.740 --> 02:20.310
Dr. Gebok?

02:20.310 --> 02:26.370
So you're the research chief of the Third Artificial Life Form R&D Lab and one of those involved in making Hyouka?

02:26.370 --> 02:27.500
That's me.

02:27.500 --> 02:28.920
I thought you died.

02:28.920 --> 02:29.740
I did.

02:29.740 --> 02:32.760
I did die, but using a fragment of my brain stem that was scientifically preserved,

02:32.760 --> 02:35.000
I transplanted myself into my extra body that was scientifically made in advance,

02:35.000 --> 02:36.680
and I was scientifically revived.

02:36.680 --> 02:38.510
So, what brings you here to us today?

02:38.510 --> 02:43.820
Of course, to check what kind of data Thirteen has accumulated in three years,

02:43.820 --> 02:45.770
since that fabulous event of Thirteen killing me without any hesitation.

02:45.770 --> 02:47.220
By the way, this is a self-destruction module.

02:47.220 --> 02:49.410
What will you do, Thirteen?

02:59.290 --> 03:00.800
Owie.

03:02.530 --> 03:03.570
Oh no.

03:04.110 --> 03:05.280
Are you all right?

03:15.290 --> 03:17.220
Yes, three years ago...

03:17.220 --> 03:21.680
It feels like there was a fourth person in that lab without any hope.

03:23.920 --> 03:25.560
Maybe I should go home.

03:25.560 --> 03:27.320
I'll probably be only a bother.

03:27.320 --> 03:30.680
It's a bother to have you standing in front of the store, ya know.

03:31.290 --> 03:31.810
I'm sorry.

03:33.600 --> 03:34.860
What's ya name?

03:34.860 --> 03:36.740
I'm Hyouka.

03:36.740 --> 03:37.820
Midarezaki Hyouka.

03:37.820 --> 03:39.320
Hyouka-yan, eh?

03:39.320 --> 03:40.610
Thanks a bunch.

03:40.610 --> 03:43.210
Ya called the ambulance for me, yeah?

03:43.210 --> 03:45.030
I heard from the hospital's doc.

03:45.030 --> 03:49.340
I don't remember much about yesterday, but I wanted to say thanks.

03:49.340 --> 03:50.160
Thanks a bunch.

03:50.870 --> 03:51.600
But...

03:52.320 --> 03:53.500
Why don't we settle down?

03:53.500 --> 03:55.250
Come on in.

03:56.000 --> 03:57.000
I can?

03:57.530 --> 04:00.760
I ain't going to get any customers coming anyways, so don't worry.

04:05.360 --> 04:07.510
My pops was a total good-for-nothing.

04:07.510 --> 04:10.120
He racked up a debt from gambling and then disappeared.

04:10.500 --> 04:14.880
I live working part-time at
the pachinko parlor and at this store, too.

04:14.880 --> 04:16.310
Ah, that's why you came from that side.

04:17.290 --> 04:19.190
Forget that. Eat up.

04:19.620 --> 04:22.580
Although, I baked them, so they might not be so good.

04:22.580 --> 04:23.200
Thank you.

04:39.080 --> 04:41.950
What the heck is this?! It's addictively fun!

04:41.950 --> 04:44.460
You don't find it gross, lassie?

04:44.460 --> 04:47.390
I always thought it's a monster-like effect.

04:47.390 --> 04:50.840
Nah. It's not scary or gross at all.

04:50.840 --> 04:52.810
In fact, it's so funny, I can't control myself.

04:52.810 --> 04:53.860
Fun?

04:55.810 --> 05:01.070
I wonder why. Every time I think of lassie,
the back of my brain hurts.

05:03.470 --> 05:05.030
Are you going out?

05:05.650 --> 05:06.870
No, not really.

05:07.390 --> 05:10.390
Well actually, just meeting someone I know.

05:10.390 --> 05:11.400
Someone he knows?

05:11.400 --> 05:12.590
Maybe his friend-

05:12.590 --> 05:13.080
Shh!

05:13.520 --> 05:15.750
Usually it's this time of the day she...

05:17.630 --> 05:19.750
Sleepy! I'm so sleepy I could die.

05:19.750 --> 05:23.990
I don't care about advancing technology in space.
Instead, create a sleepiness suction machine.

05:24.350 --> 05:25.510
What's wrong, you guys?

05:25.510 --> 05:26.800
What's with the strange looks?

05:25.510 --> 05:27.850
There's simply nothing going on.

05:27.850 --> 05:29.260
Good morning, Kyouka.

05:33.430 --> 05:36.480
I can't imagine what would happen if Kyouka found out what Hyouka's doing.

05:36.480 --> 05:38.750
Both of you, make sure to keep it a secret.

05:38.750 --> 05:39.710
You're right.

05:39.710 --> 05:40.270
Can't agree more.

06:21.150 --> 06:22.480
It's fine...

06:22.480 --> 06:24.650
It'll all work out if I persevere.

06:25.730 --> 06:28.290
My parents were always on bad terms.

06:28.290 --> 06:32.240
Whenever I was depressed over it, Yuiko-neeyan often said that phrase to me to cheer me up.

06:33.160 --> 06:35.320
Must be the girl in the photo.

06:35.320 --> 06:39.250
But Yuiko-neeyan stopped coming home one day.

06:39.250 --> 06:41.380
Things just went downhill from there.

06:41.380 --> 06:45.170
When I noticed, that bakery named Pachinko Store was all I had.

06:45.170 --> 06:46.440
Lassie...

06:46.440 --> 06:48.610
But I ain't got any time to be depressed.

06:48.610 --> 06:52.610
I gotta protect that store, or else the place for Yuiko-neeyan to come back to will disappear.

06:52.610 --> 06:56.840
If Yuiko-neeyan comes home, everything will work out.

06:57.310 --> 06:58.430
I believe it will.

06:59.380 --> 07:00.420
I wonder why.

07:00.420 --> 07:02.850
I want to protect lassie's smile.

07:02.850 --> 07:03.960
I felt the desire to.

07:05.690 --> 07:07.280
That must be first love.

07:07.280 --> 07:09.280
First Love.

07:09.280 --> 07:10.550
First love?

07:10.550 --> 07:13.850
That's right. People all become sick when they fall in love.

07:13.850 --> 07:18.070
Being lonely, having heartache without any reason,
and spacing out and not being able to think straight.

07:18.070 --> 07:19.160
Really?

07:19.160 --> 07:21.130
But being in love is great.

07:21.130 --> 07:23.740
When I had my first love-

07:25.320 --> 07:26.920
Ginichi-san! Look at you, dressed like that again!

07:26.920 --> 07:28.420
Oh no, she found me!

07:28.420 --> 07:31.120
You have to act more manly, Ginichi-san!

07:31.120 --> 07:34.710
But I have to go to work now, so forgive me.

07:31.190 --> 07:34.710
Stop running. I'll force the manly side out of your body.

07:37.870 --> 07:39.680
First love?

07:39.680 --> 07:40.890
Tamina.

07:40.890 --> 07:42.230
Yano-kun.

07:42.230 --> 07:43.270
I love you.

07:44.610 --> 07:45.480
I don't get it.

07:45.480 --> 07:49.990
I feel like I have forgotten something very important.

07:50.510 --> 07:53.040
Yes, that was three years ago.

07:53.040 --> 07:55.370
The armor's perfect. Equipped with ample weapons.

07:55.370 --> 07:58.240
It's the best biological weapon we can show anywhere.

07:58.240 --> 07:59.700
How is that so?

07:59.700 --> 08:01.750
Get on your feet, Thirteen.

08:02.790 --> 08:05.380
I said stand. Stand and fight.

08:05.380 --> 08:07.390
You're a devil made to stand, fight, and kill.

08:07.390 --> 08:09.230
That's what we created you for!

08:10.120 --> 08:12.280
Stop it. I can't do it.

08:12.280 --> 08:13.130
Stop it, Professor!

08:13.130 --> 08:18.160
Why? Given Thirteen's parameters,
this much of gravity shouldn't be anything.

08:18.160 --> 08:20.910
It must be the side effect of giving him emotions.

08:20.910 --> 08:23.400
It must have a resistance towards fighting.

08:23.400 --> 08:25.940
But overcoming that will create a true devil.

08:26.600 --> 08:30.420
Let's have him erase any hesitation towards killing.

08:41.210 --> 08:44.210
First love? What, Hyouka-yan, ya in love?

08:44.210 --> 08:46.430
Yeah, Ginka told me I am.

08:46.430 --> 08:48.530
Really, eh?

08:48.530 --> 08:51.370
I wonder who the person ya like is.

08:51.370 --> 08:52.630
The person I like?

08:55.440 --> 08:58.970
All right, if that's the case, let me do some favor for ya.

08:59.310 --> 09:00.370
What are you going to do?

09:00.370 --> 09:02.360
Do ya own any clothes?

09:02.360 --> 09:05.520
Ya shouldn't be dressed like that when ya meet the girl ya like.

09:05.520 --> 09:07.620
Ya got to dress up a little.

09:07.620 --> 09:13.820
In that case, Father told me before that if I ever needed anything, I should go to Soraborne city.

09:18.820 --> 09:21.260
Man, it's so hot. I'm gonna die.

09:20.680 --> 09:22.700
That's your second time saying that.

09:21.950 --> 09:23.580
Oo, so dramatic.

09:23.580 --> 09:26.010
We're the wind. We're going to be the wind.

09:26.750 --> 09:29.750
Wow, this place looks sketchy.

09:29.750 --> 09:31.770
More like, is this really Japan?

09:32.160 --> 09:34.700
Can't tell which shop sells clothes.

09:34.700 --> 09:35.670
Yeah.

09:35.670 --> 09:38.590
Oh dear, oh dear, oh dear, oh dear, oh dear.

09:42.700 --> 09:44.890
Um, ya all right?

09:44.890 --> 09:49.080
Oh dear, oh dear, I shall be too late to look and purchase clothes!

09:49.080 --> 09:50.980
If you're in that situation come on over to our place.

09:50.980 --> 09:55.860
Just like Alice from Alice in Wonderland,
would you like to change characters in just ten minutes?

09:55.860 --> 09:57.210
Wonderland?

09:57.210 --> 09:58.850
Opening today?

10:00.010 --> 10:01.080
Here it is.

10:03.190 --> 10:04.120
Welcome.

10:14.360 --> 10:15.630
Welcome guests.

10:15.630 --> 10:16.980
My name is Jabberwocky.

10:16.980 --> 10:21.340
I am the devil who thrives on catastrophe, sitting on the throne of destruction.

10:21.340 --> 10:24.680
I do not know where you came from, but you're out of luck!

10:24.680 --> 10:26.560
What are you doing, Mother?

10:26.560 --> 10:29.640
Hey, don't spoil the fun! You noticed it was me too fast, Hyouka.

10:29.640 --> 10:33.570
You're being very annoying and bothersome,
so it'd make me glad if you would head home.

10:33.570 --> 10:37.400
You think this Kyouka-sama would head home without doing anything when such an interesting event is going on?

10:37.400 --> 10:38.950
Nice to meet you, lassie.

10:38.950 --> 10:41.880
Thank you for your support for my son.

10:42.750 --> 10:43.570
Son?

10:43.570 --> 10:44.330
And mother?

10:44.330 --> 10:49.780
However, judging from the information my familiar has brought me, your kind acts seems to be a little off the mark.

10:50.500 --> 10:52.630
You called us, Kyouka-sama?

10:52.630 --> 10:54.460
What's this? It's disgusting.

10:54.460 --> 10:56.260
Don't call it that.

10:56.260 --> 11:01.340
That's Kyouka-sama avatar, my ultra-small fake body controlled through Cellphone.

11:01.340 --> 11:03.800
Call it Petit Kyouka-sama.

11:03.800 --> 11:04.470
You're given permission to!

11:04.470 --> 11:10.300
That Ouka thinks he faked it well, but I noticed you acting strangely recently,

11:10.300 --> 11:12.800
so I've been monitoring you using Petit Kyouka-sama.

11:12.800 --> 11:13.730
Talk about trouble.

11:13.730 --> 11:18.030
Allow me, the omniscient and omnipotent god,
to coordinate your clothes.

11:18.030 --> 11:18.860
Everyone go!

11:18.860 --> 11:20.750
Kyouka! Kyouka!

11:20.750 --> 11:23.370
Kyouka! Kyouka! Kyouka!

11:23.710 --> 11:26.590
It's fine, Mother. Please leave me alone.

11:27.600 --> 11:28.720
Don't worry about it.

11:28.720 --> 11:31.830
I didn't come cosplayed for nothing.

11:31.830 --> 11:35.150
I must match my character and outfit!

11:32.570 --> 11:34.580
No, don't go in there!

11:35.150 --> 11:37.590
Looks like I wasn't needed.

11:38.270 --> 11:40.970
This is getting interesting.

11:46.470 --> 11:47.970
Sign: Her Heart is a Black Box
Operation You'll Never Find Out Unless You Ask Her Out

11:47.160 --> 11:47.970
And so!

11:47.970 --> 11:51.350
To cheer on Hyouka, I demand that the entire Midarezaki take part!

11:51.350 --> 11:53.150
We'll start: Her Heart is a Black Box!

11:53.150 --> 11:56.190
Operation You Will Never Find Out Unless You Ask Her Out!

11:56.760 --> 11:58.650
Looks like she knew everything.

11:58.650 --> 12:00.570
Why does she have to make things so extravagant all the time?

12:00.570 --> 12:01.640
The rules are simple.

12:01.640 --> 12:06.070
To Hyouka, who gives you his words of love, you will act on the response written on the paper you draw from this box.

12:06.070 --> 12:09.610
So it's a confession simulation game to increase Hyouka's relationship level!

12:09.610 --> 12:11.620
Allow me to start...

12:13.950 --> 12:15.050
This one.

12:15.050 --> 12:16.000
All right, Hyouka.

12:16.000 --> 12:18.100
"I love you." "I like you." "I want you."

12:18.100 --> 12:20.590
Say any sweet words that come to mind.

12:20.590 --> 12:21.510
Come on!

12:21.510 --> 12:22.540
Uhhh....

12:22.540 --> 12:23.510
I like you.

12:23.510 --> 12:24.510
Die!

12:25.470 --> 12:29.000
That was a situation where lassie is an assassin from some country...

12:29.000 --> 12:32.870
...and has to kill anyone who asks her out in case it interferes with her work.

12:32.870 --> 12:34.730
What is with that unreasonable situation?!

12:34.730 --> 12:37.510
You never know what will happen in life!

12:37.510 --> 12:39.500
Next up, Yuuka!

12:41.030 --> 12:43.730
Um, um... I don't think I can do it well.

12:43.730 --> 12:45.490
Don't worry, it's just a game.

12:46.550 --> 12:47.990
Okay...

12:47.990 --> 12:48.630
This one.

12:56.440 --> 12:58.630
I'm ready, Hyouka.

12:58.630 --> 12:59.910
I like you.

13:03.880 --> 13:05.490
Yup, it says it right here.

13:05.490 --> 13:06.840
To kiss from being ecstatic.

13:06.840 --> 13:09.260
I think this is pretty unreasonable, too.

13:13.740 --> 13:14.520
Yuuka!

13:14.520 --> 13:16.060
Hyouka, what are you doing?!

13:17.380 --> 13:23.320
The inhalation system took Yuuka as meat and sucked her in automatically.

13:23.320 --> 13:25.300
Spit her out right now!

13:25.300 --> 13:25.820
Spit!

13:26.900 --> 13:28.460
Are you all right, Yuuka?

13:30.240 --> 13:31.990
Well, moving on!

13:31.990 --> 13:33.460
We're still doing this?

13:33.460 --> 13:37.460
Of course! Forget about Yuuka, who died in action with honor, for a moment!

13:37.460 --> 13:39.480
I hope I'm not next.

13:39.480 --> 13:40.520
Me, too.

13:40.870 --> 13:42.430
I hope it's not me.

13:45.670 --> 13:47.220
Hey, it's lassie.

13:47.220 --> 13:48.210
Good evening.

13:48.210 --> 13:50.400
The very person who is here is the special guest!

13:51.220 --> 13:52.840
So you're the one Hyouka's been seeing?

13:52.840 --> 13:58.860
I'm sorry. I rang the bell but didn't get an answer, so I let myself in.

13:58.860 --> 14:00.710
How very convenient.

14:00.710 --> 14:03.100
Let's have you join this party.

14:03.100 --> 14:05.440
With the very person we're doing this for, Hyouka's bound to gain experience.

14:05.440 --> 14:07.690
Take a paper out of this box.

14:09.280 --> 14:10.280
Hyouka, now's your chance to get away!

14:10.280 --> 14:11.080
Yeah.

14:11.670 --> 14:13.550
Lassie, this way.

14:14.910 --> 14:15.500
Hyouka-yan?

14:15.500 --> 14:17.030
Hey, wait!

14:17.030 --> 14:18.120
What are you all thinking?

14:18.120 --> 14:21.750
Depending on the answer you give,
I shall send you to the sewer personally.

14:18.120 --> 14:19.820
Just behave yourself!

14:19.820 --> 14:21.750
It's up to them from here on.

14:21.750 --> 14:26.130
We shouldn't intefere and just see how they go.

14:26.130 --> 14:28.520
No! That's boring!

14:28.520 --> 14:30.760
Oh, that made the knot tighter.

14:30.760 --> 14:32.950
That was embarrassing.

14:32.950 --> 14:35.630
Nah, not at all. It's nice to have such a lively family.

14:35.630 --> 14:37.140
They all looked like fun people.

14:37.140 --> 14:39.120
In any case, what brings you here all of a sudden?

14:39.120 --> 14:43.150
Well, actually... I came to apologize to you.

14:43.150 --> 14:44.690
Apologize? Regarding what?

14:44.690 --> 14:49.530
Today... in fact, for the past couple of days, I'm sorry I made ya work for me.

14:49.530 --> 14:52.150
Ya don't act like it's a bother,
so I kept taking advantage of ya.

14:52.500 --> 14:53.350
Really...

14:54.270 --> 14:56.330
I'm such a worthless girl.

14:56.330 --> 14:59.050
I'm the one who had you do things for me.

14:59.050 --> 15:01.130
You always-

15:00.660 --> 15:01.710
No...

15:01.710 --> 15:05.530
The reason why I spent time with ya was all for myself.

15:05.530 --> 15:06.650
What do you mean?

15:06.650 --> 15:12.260
I've been alone since Yuiko-neeyan disappeared and my family broke apart.

15:12.600 --> 15:14.930
And ya appeared right when all of this was happening.

15:14.930 --> 15:16.870
I was lonely.

15:16.870 --> 15:21.130
So I thought ya might become my friend if I acted nice to ya.

15:21.530 --> 15:22.190
So...

15:22.690 --> 15:25.190
I'm the one who needed ya.

15:25.190 --> 15:29.570
But I see very well that you didn't need me.

15:29.570 --> 15:34.200
You're lucky to have a family that calls you by your name.

15:34.890 --> 15:35.780
Lassie...

15:35.780 --> 15:39.010
My name's Takanashi Kiriko.

15:39.010 --> 15:40.000
But I've not been called that once...

15:40.440 --> 15:42.530
Not even by my parents...

15:43.660 --> 15:47.880
You know, I'm not too good at speaking, so I can't say it well,

15:47.880 --> 15:50.140
but I like you.

15:51.990 --> 15:55.880
You need someone to help, and I want to help you, and not as a favor.

15:55.880 --> 15:59.310
I just wish you to be smiling.

15:59.310 --> 16:00.130
Hyouka-yan...

16:02.430 --> 16:03.610
What's going on?

16:05.810 --> 16:08.070
Ciao. It's a trespasser.

16:08.070 --> 16:09.860
Who's that creep?

16:09.860 --> 16:10.820
Dr. Gebok!

16:10.820 --> 16:14.220
Gebok! You still haven't given up on Hyouka?

16:14.220 --> 16:21.060
Of course not. With Hell-chan and Saruwatari-kun gone, it is my job to oversee Black Thirteen's development.

16:21.060 --> 16:24.460
Besides, we seem to luckily have our next sacrifice.

16:25.460 --> 16:26.440
Sacrifice?

16:26.440 --> 16:28.150
Oh? You don't know what I'm talking about?

16:28.150 --> 16:30.590
It happened three years ago.

16:30.590 --> 16:31.970
Three years ago?

16:34.260 --> 16:35.460
Hyouka-yan?

16:35.460 --> 16:38.050
That's right. There was...

16:40.160 --> 16:43.040
There was a girl next to me.

17:06.040 --> 17:10.210
And one day, I was practicing shooting like always.

17:14.300 --> 17:20.360
That's right! You shot her! You shot the target without knowing your friend was inside!

17:20.360 --> 17:20.930
Into pieces!

17:21.830 --> 17:22.680
What did you say?

17:22.680 --> 17:25.280
Killing one or two is the same thing.

17:25.610 --> 17:29.100
Kill one, and the resistance to killing will reduce.

17:29.100 --> 17:31.150
That girl was a sacrifice I prepared for that purpose.

17:31.150 --> 17:32.780
Her name was, if I remember...

17:33.210 --> 17:35.070
Right, Takanashi Yuiko.

17:38.990 --> 17:40.450
No. It's not true.

17:40.450 --> 17:42.200
Hyouka-yan killed Nee-yan?

17:42.200 --> 17:43.200
How heartless of him.

17:43.200 --> 17:45.820
Recognized experiments come with sacrifices.

17:45.820 --> 17:49.220
Thanks to the event, Thirteen went berserk even more than we expected.

17:49.220 --> 17:52.390
Of course, as a result, I died.

17:52.390 --> 17:56.720
I guess no one can be freed from their cursed destiny.

17:57.720 --> 18:02.220
I'll have you become a sacrifice for completing Black Thirteen, as well.

18:03.640 --> 18:05.120
That rotten scumbag!

18:05.120 --> 18:05.640
I won't forgive you!

18:05.640 --> 18:06.980
I'll lend a hand, as well!

18:06.980 --> 18:08.570
Hold on a minute, Kyouka, Teika.

18:08.570 --> 18:11.770
Ouka! You're not telling us not to fight in this situation, are you?!

18:12.240 --> 18:14.200
This is Hyouka's battle.

18:14.200 --> 18:15.290
We must keep out of it.

18:15.290 --> 18:21.030
Well, I wonder what kind of data Thirteen will show me when I kill you.

18:22.280 --> 18:23.540
Stop it...

18:23.540 --> 18:25.660
Don't touch lassie!

18:26.830 --> 18:28.620
What if I said I will?

18:28.620 --> 18:30.290
Come on out, everyone!

18:44.620 --> 18:45.190
This is!

18:45.190 --> 18:47.060
Gebok!

18:47.060 --> 18:48.590
Amazing!

18:53.440 --> 18:55.790
It's okay now, lassie.

19:00.890 --> 19:04.240
"It's fine. It'll all work out if I persevere."

19:05.370 --> 19:09.680
What could I expect? I'm the one that stole her one and only hope.

19:09.680 --> 19:10.580
Hyouka...

19:11.280 --> 19:14.040
What does it take for me to be forgiven?

19:14.590 --> 19:17.220
What does it take for me to atone for this sin?

19:18.590 --> 19:22.090
Is being killed the only way to clear the sin of killing others?

19:22.090 --> 19:26.100
If so, kill me. Kill me, lassie.

19:26.930 --> 19:32.360
It might have all started with me having wild imaginations, but I still like you.

19:32.360 --> 19:33.270
So forgive me.

19:33.610 --> 19:34.720
Forgive me...

19:35.140 --> 19:36.620
Don't hate me...

19:40.620 --> 19:42.270
I feel bad for Hyouka.

19:42.270 --> 19:43.360
I can't bear to watch him.

19:43.360 --> 19:46.250
But there's nothing we can do about it.

19:47.630 --> 19:49.620
Are you sure about that?

20:05.140 --> 20:08.140
Love letter. Love letter.

20:08.140 --> 20:10.090
Here's today's weather.

20:10.490 --> 20:13.640
You'll see the sun all over the capital area.

20:14.110 --> 20:19.300
The chance of rain is 10%, and the great weather should last the rest of the day.

20:16.050 --> 20:17.290
Is no one home?

20:19.980 --> 20:22.820
This weather also seems to last for a while.

20:20.750 --> 20:22.820
Hey, we have a guest.

20:22.820 --> 20:25.820
Gosh, where did everyone go?

20:29.060 --> 20:30.100
Lassie!

20:30.100 --> 20:31.500
I am angry.

20:31.500 --> 20:33.180
I'm very angry.

20:34.500 --> 20:36.080
Damn shit face!

20:36.670 --> 20:38.360
What is this all of a sudden?

20:38.360 --> 20:40.490
Ya gave me a letter.

20:40.490 --> 20:41.370
Letter?

20:42.330 --> 20:43.300
Why do you have that?

20:43.850 --> 20:47.230
Yeah, the other day, I was in such a panic that I ran home.

20:47.230 --> 20:48.600
I shouldn't have. I'm sorry.

20:48.600 --> 20:51.280
But ya also suffered.

20:51.280 --> 20:53.510
Yet what do ya mean, "I'm sorry"?

20:53.510 --> 20:56.110
What do ya mean, "Forgive me"?
What do you mean, "Don't hate me"?

20:56.110 --> 20:57.280
Don't make a fool out of me!

20:57.280 --> 20:59.610
There isn't a single reason for ya to apologize, too!

21:00.900 --> 21:01.930
Lassie...

21:04.040 --> 21:06.910
I've calmed down a lot since then and thought about lots of stuff.

21:06.910 --> 21:09.330
I decided to leave this city.

21:10.080 --> 21:11.220
Leave?

21:12.050 --> 21:15.040
I don't have a reason to protect that store anymore.

21:15.040 --> 21:20.540
I'm going to leave the city to give myself a chance to see who I am and think how I should live.

21:20.540 --> 21:24.520
Not as the lassie of the Pachinko Store,
but as Takanashi Kiriko.

21:26.550 --> 21:31.210
So let's meet again when I've gained the confidence to be Takanashi Kiriko.

21:31.210 --> 21:34.560
Ya, the first person who said he likes me.

21:35.560 --> 21:40.310
The person ya said ya liked was me, wasn't it?

21:41.690 --> 21:43.280
Yeah, I think so.

21:43.580 --> 21:44.420
Ya think?

21:44.930 --> 21:46.320
That's fine for now.

21:46.320 --> 21:49.320
Call me whenever you're in trouble. I'll fly over.

21:49.320 --> 21:51.330
Yup. Thanks.

21:54.380 --> 21:55.820
I'll see you again, Hyouka-yan.

21:58.270 --> 22:00.740
Good luck, Takanashi Kiriko-san.

22:21.050 --> 22:22.000
Listen pigs!

22:22.000 --> 22:24.330
Even if it's unsightly, struggle, fight, and stand!

22:24.330 --> 22:27.980
But of course, I do things very elegantly all the time,
so none of the above applies to me.

23:40.110 --> 23:42.170
*sob sob* *sob sob*

23:42.170 --> 23:44.870
What's wrong, Yuuka-chan? Why are you crying?

23:44.870 --> 23:47.020
Because... Because...

23:47.020 --> 23:48.700
You'll simply understand if you watch next week's airing.

23:48.700 --> 23:51.650
Next time on Kyouran Kazoku Nikki Extra.

23:51.650 --> 23:53.360
Pick up a Cat on Monday.
